# Ezmerelda d'Avenir camped by Van Richten's Tower on Lake Baratok (docs/voice/ezmerelda.md; her Tarokka join is the
# abbey's). She is here when the cards did not name her. Her trust (ezmerelda_trust) rises with the letter, the
# truth about Rudolph, the den; it falls if the party robs her wagon, lies badly or leaves Kiril on top.

~ start
if guest:rictavio and not flag.van_richten_reunited
-> reunion_guest
endif
if flag.van_richten_reunited
-> reunited
endif
if flag.ezmerelda_wagon_robbed and not flag.ezmerelda_robbery_noticed
-> robbed
endif
if not flag.ezmerelda_met_at_tower
-> first_meeting
endif
Ezmerelda: Back again. Has the tower spoken to you yet? It won't speak to me.
-> menu

~ first_meeting
set ezmerelda_met_at_tower
set ezmerelda_met
if not quest.the_hunters_tower
quest the_hunters_tower heard
endif
Narrator: By a painted wagon, a woman in a long dark coat sits fixing silver heads to crossbow bolts. Below her right knee, a brace of oak and steel; her left hand is bandaged, and she smells faintly of burnt hair.
Narrator: She doesn't look up. She lifts a small loaded crossbow off her knee instead and points it at you.
Ezmerelda: Stop there. Say something a vampire wouldn't say.
* Your fire's lovely. Nice and bright. -> hello_fire
* Is that silver? We'll have some, if you're selling. -> hello_silver

~ hello_fire
Ezmerelda [smile]: A vampire would have said something about my eyes. Fine. Sit down before you fall in the lake.
-> menu

~ hello_silver
Ezmerelda: Nobody with fangs has ever asked to buy silver. Not twice, anyway. Sit.
-> menu

~ menu
* Who are you? -> who
* What's wrong with the tower? -> tower
* What happened to your hand? -> hand
* [if flag.ezmerelda_trap_found] You trapped your own wagon. -> trap_talk
* [if (flag.van_richten_identity_known or flag.rictavio_unmasked) and not flag.van_richten_reunited and not flag.ezmerelda_told_rictavio and not flag.ezmerelda_secret_kept and not flag.ezmerelda_lied] We know where Van Richten is. -> where
* [if flag.van_richten_letter_found and not flag.ezmerelda_given_letter] We found a letter in the tower, with your name on it. -> letter
* [if not flag.pack_resolved] What do you know about the wolves in these hills? -> wolves
* [if flag.pack_resolved and not flag.ezmerelda_heard_den] The pack in the hills is settled. -> den_news
* [if flag.ezmerelda_trust >= 2 and not guest:ezmerelda] Hunt with us. -> join
* Goodbye. -> bye

~ who
Ezmerelda: Ezmerelda d'Avenir. Vistani, when the wagons will have me. I hunt the things that hunt people. Right now I'm hunting one stubborn old man who taught me how, and who has locked me out of his house.
interject background:sage: d'Avenir. Van Richten's student. You're in his second monograph, on the hunting of werewolves.
Ezmerelda: He'll have got my good side wrong.
-> menu

~ tower
set khazan_known
if not flag.ezmerelda_asked_in
set ezmerelda_asked_in
if not quest.the_hunters_tower or quest.the_hunters_tower == heard
quest the_hunters_tower asked
endif
endif
Ezmerelda: It's Rudolph's. Rudolph van Richten. An archmage built it centuries ago, and the old lock still opens to that wizard's name. I found the name under the moss in an hour: KHAZAN.
Ezmerelda: Then Rudolph's own ward threw me twenty feet into the lake. He wove my name into it. Mine. Nobody else's. Months of work, to keep out one person.
if name:kip_smudgewick
interject name:kip_smudgewick: A ward keyed to one named party? That's a very specific clause. Somebody wrote that very carefully.
else
interject tag:scholarly: A ward keyed to a single person? That's extraordinary craft.
endif
Ezmerelda: He was always thorough about the wrong things.
Ezmerelda: It won't know you. Go in for me. Find out where he's gone, and bring me anything with his handwriting on it.
if treasure_at:van_richtens_tower
Ezmerelda: And there's a strongbox in his lantern room he never let me near. He called what was in it "the thing the cards keep moving". Eva would know what that means. So, I suspect, do you.
endif
* We'll go in. -> tower_yes
* What's in it for us? -> tower_price

~ tower_yes
Ezmerelda: Good. Say the name, mind your feet, and don't touch anything that hums. He likes things that hum.
-> menu

~ tower_price
Ezmerelda: Whatever he's left lying about that isn't his notes. He'll be appalled. That's a reward in itself.
-> menu

~ hand
Ezmerelda: The ward. It knows my name; it also knows my temper. We had words. It won.
-> menu

~ trap_talk
Ezmerelda: Of course I trapped it. There's a werewolf pack two hours up the ridge, and a castle that reads over everyone's shoulder. You found it. Good eyes. Most people find it with their faces.
-> menu

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Where is Rudolph?

~ where
Narrator: She puts the crossbow down, which she hasn't done since you arrived.
Ezmerelda: Where?
* He's at the Blue Water Inn in Vallaki, calling himself Rictavio. -> tell
* [if flag.rictavio_secret_kept] We promised him we'd keep his secret. -> keep
* He's alive. He doesn't want to be found. That's all we'll say. -> keep
* [Deception DC 15] We were wrong. We don't know where he is. -> lie_ok | lie_fail

~ tell
set ezmerelda_told_rictavio
set ezmerelda_trust += 1
if quest.the_hunters_tower != reunited and not flag.rictavio_gone
quest the_hunters_tower told
endif
Ezmerelda: Rictavio. Rudolph is calling himself Rictavio. In a taproom.
if flag.rictavio_secret_kept
if name:godrick_pendlebrook
interject name:godrick_pendlebrook: We gave him our word. And now we've broken it. I don't like that, madam. Not one bit.
else
interject tag:loyal: We gave him our word. That's broken now.
endif
Ezmerelda: Then I'll tell him I wrung it out of you. He'll believe it. He knows me.
endif
if flag.rictavio_gone
Ezmerelda: Wait. If he'd left Vallaki, where would he go to lick his wounds? Where would he go that I couldn't follow?
Narrator: She turns, slowly, and looks out across the water at the tower with the one lit window.
Ezmerelda: He's in there. He came home. He's been in there the whole time, listening to me shout.
-> trust_check
endif
Ezmerelda: Feathers? Tell me there are feathers. No, don't. I'll see for myself. I'm leaving tonight.
set ezmerelda_left_tower
-> trust_check

~ keep
set ezmerelda_secret_kept
if quest.the_hunters_tower != reunited
quest the_hunters_tower kept
endif
Ezmerelda [angry]: He made you promise. Of course he did. He's very good at making people promise things that keep them away from him.
Ezmerelda: ...Fine. Keep his secret. You're the first people in this valley who've kept anything. I'll keep looking. I'm good at looking.
-> menu

~ lie_ok
set ezmerelda_lied
Narrator: She looks at you for a long moment, and decides to believe you. It costs her something.
Ezmerelda: Then I'll keep waiting. I'm good at waiting. No, I'm not. I'm terrible at it.
-> menu

~ lie_fail
set ezmerelda_lied
set ezmerelda_trust -= 1
Ezmerelda: You're a terrible liar. He made you promise, didn't he. He always makes people promise.
-> menu

~ letter
set ezmerelda_given_letter
set ezmerelda_trust += 1
Narrator: She breaks the seal with her thumb and reads it twice, and then folds it very small and puts it inside her coat, against her chest.
Ezmerelda: "If you are reading this, I am dead, or you are more stubborn than I hoped." I am more stubborn. I am always more stubborn. He knows that. He wrote it anyway.
-> trust_check

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- The wolves

~ wolves
set den_way_known
if not quest.wolves_in_the_hills
quest wolves_in_the_hills heard
endif
Ezmerelda: A pack dens two hours east along the ridge, in a cave above Lake Zarovich. One of them took my leg below the knee, years ago, when I was young and quick and stupid. Big, black, and laughing while it did it.
Ezmerelda: I've been taking them back two at a time ever since. Lately they've been carrying children up there, from the farms under Krezk. I'd go in after them, if Rudolph would let me into his armoury.
if name:thistle
interject name:thistle: Two at a time? Wolves don't wait their turn. Hit the den all at once.
else
interject class:fighter: Two at a time is how you lose. All at once is how you win.
endif
Ezmerelda: Says someone who still has both feet.
-> menu

~ den_news
set ezmerelda_heard_den
if flag.wolf_pack_leader == "kiril"
set ezmerelda_trust -= 1
Ezmerelda [angry]: Kiril. Big, black, laughs with his mouth open? You left that one on top? With the children?
if flag.den_children_freed
Ezmerelda: You got the children out, at least. I'll give you that. I'll give you that and nothing else.
endif
-> menu
endif
Ezmerelda: Kiril. Big, black, laughs with his mouth open?
Narrator: You tell her. She listens without moving, and when you're done she lets out a long breath, as if she has been holding it for twelve years.
Ezmerelda: That's the one who took my leg. Thank you. I wanted to do it myself. I find I don't mind that much, now.
set ezmerelda_trust += 1
if flag.den_children_freed
set ezmerelda_trust += 1
Ezmerelda: And the children are going home. Good. That's a better day than this valley usually allows.
endif
if flag.wolf_pack_leader == "emil"
Ezmerelda: A pack that leaves people alone. I'll believe it when I've watched it for a year.
endif
-> trust_check

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Trust, gifts, the hunt

~ trust_check
if flag.ezmerelda_trust >= 2 and not flag.ezmerelda_gift_given
set ezmerelda_gift_given
Ezmerelda: Here. You've earned better than thanks. Silver-headed bolts, holy water and my last good potion. Don't waste them on anything that doesn't deserve them.
give holy_water 2
give potion_of_healing 1
give crossbow_bolt 10
endif
if flag.ezmerelda_left_tower
Ezmerelda: Now go away. I have a wagon to hitch and an old man to shout at.
-> END
endif
-> menu

~ join
if tarokka.ally.npc == ezmerelda
Ezmerelda: Eva's cards, I suppose. They've been dealing me into other people's games since I was six. Fine.
else
Ezmerelda: I hunt alone. Usually. But you've done more for me in a week than the whole valley has in a year. All right. Until it's done.
endif
join ezmerelda
Ezmerelda: I go first through doors, I take the silver, and nobody calls me "girl".
-> END

~ robbed
set ezmerelda_robbery_noticed
set ezmerelda_trust -= 2
set ezmerelda_met_at_tower
set ezmerelda_met
Ezmerelda [angry]: Somebody has been in my wagon. Don't. Don't say anything. I know who's been up and down this shore this week, and it's a very short list.
Ezmerelda: Keep what you took. You'll need it. And then stay out of my way.
-> menu

~ bye
Ezmerelda: Go carefully. If anything in these hills hums, growls or compliments you, shoot it.
-> END

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Rudolph arrives with the party

~ reunion_guest
set ezmerelda_met_at_tower
set ezmerelda_met
Narrator: The woman by the wagon looks up from her bolts, sees who is walking behind you, and goes completely still.
Ezmerelda: Rudolph. You're wearing feathers.
Rictavio: It's a costume. It's a very good costume.
Ezmerelda: It's a terrible costume. You look like a chicken that's been to a wedding. You keyed your ward to me.
Rictavio: Everyone I have ever taught is in the ground, Ezmerelda. You are the last. I would like you to stay the last.
Ezmerelda: Then you should have stayed alive near me, so you could keep an eye on me. That was always the deal.
Narrator: Neither of them says anything for a while. Then she hits him on the arm, hard, and he lets her.
-> reunited_set

~ reunited_set
set van_richten_reunited
set ezmerelda_trust += 2
set khazan_known
quest the_hunters_tower reunited
-> trust_check

~ reunited
Ezmerelda: He's making tea. He's terrible at tea. Don't tell him; he thinks it's the only thing he's good at besides killing.
-> menu
